@baseUrl = http://localhost:3003/api

### 1. Create a new user (4.15)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "kimmob",
  "name": "Kimmob",
  "password": "secretpassword2"
}

### 2. Get all users with populated blogs (4.15, 4.17)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users

### 3. Login to get a JWT token (4.18)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "kimmoh",
  "password": "secretpassword"
}

### 4. Get all blogs with populated user info (4.1, 4.17)
GET {{baseUrl}}/blogs

### 5. Create a new blog post using the login token (4.19)
# @name createBlog
POST {{baseUrl}}/blogs
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{
  "title": "Canonical string reduction part2",
  "author": "Edsger W. Dijkstra",
  "url": "http://www.cs.utexas.edu/~EWD/transcriptions/EWD08xx/EWD808.html",
  "likes": 12
}

### 6. Update likes on the newly created blog (4.14)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/blogs/{{createBlog.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Canonical string reduction",
  "author": "Edsger W. Dijkstra",
  "url": "http://www.cs.utexas.edu/~EWD/transcriptions/EWD08xx/EWD808.html",
  "likes": 13
}

### 7. Delete the newly created blog as its creator (4.13, 4.21)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/blogs/{{createBlog.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 8. Verify 401 Unauthorized when creating a blog without a token
POST {{baseUrl}}/blogs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Should fail without token",
  "author": "Anonymous",
  "url": "https://example.com"
}

### 9. Verify 400 Bad Request when title or url is missing (4.12)
POST {{baseUrl}}/blogs
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{
  "author": "Missing Title and URL"
}